{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["NAVC1.18", "NAVC1.63"],
      "nets": ["Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)", "GND"],
      "observed": "Both VSS pins of the NAVC MCU (pins 18 and 63) sit on a private auto-named net, Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18), that has no other connection. This net is not the GND net. The FCC1 VSS pins (10, 26, 49, 74, 99) and the other ground pins are on GND.",
      "expected": "Every VSS pin of the STM32F405 (NAVC1) must be tied to the GND plane. Without that, the NAVC MCU has no ground reference.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"92\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"63\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"10\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"power_in\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The NAVC MCU has its ground pins floating, so it cannot run or communicate reliably. Its supply and signal references are undefined.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["NAVC1", "FCC1"],
      "pins": ["NAVC1.19", "NAVC1.32", "NAVC1.48", "NAVC1.64", "FCC1.11", "FCC1.27", "FCC1.50", "FCC1.75", "FCC1.100"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)", "unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "All VDD pins of both MCUs are marked unconnected. The +3V3 net, which carries the MCU decoupling capacitors, contains no MCU VDD pin and no regulator output.",
      "expected": "All VDD pins of each STM32 must be connected to the 3.3 V MCU supply rail, which is decoupled by the capacitors on +3V3.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors) | ST LD39200PU33R"}
      ],
      "impact": "The MCUs would have no core supply, so the board would not boot. The problem may be an export artefact, but as written the design is not powered.",
      "confidence": 0.2
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V"],
      "observed": "PCA9685 address pin A0 (pin 1) is tied to the +3.3V net, while A1 to A5 are tied to GND. This gives I2C address 0x41, not the 0x40 stated in the spec. The INA219 (U1) is also at 0x40 on the same I2C2 bus.",
      "expected": "The spec lists the PCA9685 at I2C addr 0x40, which requires A0 to be on GND. Either way, the address must be consistent with the spec and must not collide with other devices on the bus.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A0\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"}
      ],
      "impact": "The firmware addressing the servo driver at 0x40 would get no response. The PCA9685 would only answer at 0x41.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The NAVC MCU's VSS pins are isolated on a private net rather than tied to GND, which is a clear open-connection fault. The MCU VDD pins are also unconnected, and the PCA9685 address strap contradicts the spec, but these are less certain."
}

